Except for the Whatsaaaa identity artwork and the third-party material named
below, the contents of this repository, the design tokens, the stylesheets, the
scripts, the <ws-ghost> element, the theme, shortcut and code-theme modules and
the docs theme among them, are provided under the MIT License that follows.

The Whatsaaaa identity artwork is excluded from the MIT License. It is
Copyright (c) 2026 Whatsaaaa, all rights reserved. It is the ghost, the
wordmark, the lockups and marks, the sprite and mark of each project, the README
headers, the social cards and the favicons, as the generated files in `assets/`,
as the drawings encoded in `src/identity/` and `identity/`, and as those
drawings compiled into the package in `dist/identity/` and `dist/ghost/`. The
code that turns those drawings into files and markup is under the MIT License;
the drawings are not.

The MIT License covers the code of the <ws-ghost> element and of the docs theme,
not the ghost they draw, and grants no right to show it. A site that is not
Whatsaaaa's own and uses either of them removes the ghost or replaces it with
its own drawing: it does not use <ws-ghost>, `ghostSvg` or `ghostMarkup`, and in
the docs theme it replaces the theme's `NavGhost.vue` and `NotFound.vue` with
its own components, the way VitePress overrides an internal component of a
theme, with a Vite alias.

Third-party material keeps its own license: the Rosé Pine palette (MIT) and the
Departure Mono glyphs (SIL Open Font License 1.1), in `licenses/`, and the
JetBrains Mono and Inter fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1), whose licenses the
build copies next to them in `dist/fonts/`.

